# App-authored briefing, not from a tape. Grounded only in
# library/reference/focus-levels-overview.md, a circulated
# summary of unclear origin. No tape or manual in the library describes Focus
# 11. The body therefore identifies the overview as a secondary map and gives
# the listener a proposition to test; it does not promote that map to fact.
# Replace or amend it when attributed experience supplies better footing.

@segment     briefing-f11
@title       Focus 11 — The Access Channel
@levels      F11
@verbosity   2
@protected   Focus 11
@duration    ~1m

say You are now in Focus 11.
pause 5
say No tape or manual in this library describes this level. The available map is a secondary overview of uncertain origin, so hold its description lightly.
pause 6
say That overview calls Focus 11 the Access Channel. It associates the level with directing physical, mental, and emotional functions, and with access to the Total Self.
pause 8
say Treat that as a proposition to test, not a result to reproduce.
pause 6
say Observe what is actually present for you, without forcing it to match the map.
pause 12
say Remember what you notice. Your attributed account may confirm, amend, or reject what the overview says.
pause 10
